Subject: [PATCH] docs: finish the fixes whose examples and gates were left
 stale
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Four of these are my own incomplete follow-through from earlier in this PR —
the logic was corrected but the example, the exit gate, or the second copy of
the rule was not.

- CODING_STANDARDS.md still listed three must-fix classes while AGENTS.md had
  moved to four, so the generated harness files carried both rules. Aligned,
  with a note that the two must stay identical, plus an explicit statement
  that Sonar severity ranks urgency and does not override the four classes.
  review.md's Blocker/Critical list now routes through the same test.
- verify.md's exit gate still demanded a branch-wide `gh run list` after Step 3
  was moved to the merge commit, so the mandatory evidence check could be
  satisfied by an unrelated green run. Now commit-scoped, completed + success.
- verify.md's deployment check used `git rev-parse HEAD`, which is the newest
  commit on master, not the merge being verified. Uses $MERGE_SHA from Step 3.
- rollback.md's two worked examples still printed `git revert -m 1` after the
  logic above them was fixed, reproducing the exact mainline error.
- greptile-resolve.sh `list --unresolved` returns every unresolved thread,
  including humans and other bots, and review.md treated the whole list as
  Greptile feedback. Kept the full listing (you need the true count) but
  flagged non-Greptile authors in the output and told /review to answer those
  individually and never bulk-resolve them.

Found by codex review on PR #132.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
