 Read at review time (the `code-review` skill loads this file) and before writing anything under `convex/`.
 Consolidated from 15 always-loaded rule files that used to sit in `.claude/rules/`.
 
-**Review feedback is advisory** except secrets, injection, and a broken build — and it never expands the PR. Anything else worth doing becomes a follow-up issue, not more commits on this branch. (Pre-user shipping regime, decided 2026-08-16. This repo has no reviewer-bot config file; the rule lives here.)
+**Review feedback is advisory** except four classes that must be fixed in the active PR: secrets, injection, a broken build, and **documentation that asserts something the code does not do**. Anything else worth doing becomes a follow-up issue, not more commits on this branch. (Pre-user shipping regime, decided 2026-08-16. This repo has no reviewer-bot config file; the rule lives here — it must stay identical to the "Shipping regime" bullet in `AGENTS.md`.)
+
+Sonar and other scanners are graded on the same four classes, not on their own severity labels: a Blocker that is a real build break or injection gets fixed here, a Blocker that is an advisory code-quality finding gets filed. Severity says how much it matters, not who fixes it when.
 
